optogenetic therapy. These results will provide a multiscale analysis providing crucial insights into how the nature of retina-based vision restoration affects its efficacy.","amount":180000,"currency":"CAD","year":2024,"start":null,"end":null,"recipients":[{"id":"I2802654988","name":"Princess Margaret Cancer Centre","country":"CA"}],"parents":[],"funder":"Fondation Brain Canada","scheme":"Capacity building grants — Canadian Cancer Society Training Grants","type":"grant","topic":null,"source":"https://braincanada.ca/funded-grants/project-overview-retina-based-optogenetic-therapy-is-a-promising-approach-to-restore-vision-to-individuals-suffering-from-retinal-degeneration-after-photoreceptor-degeneration-optogenetics-are-targeted-to-remaining-retinal-neurons-that-are-not-intrinsically-light-sensitive-in-order-to-make-them-light-responsive-however-due-to-technical-reasons-the-nature-of-light-responses-in-the-retina-following-optogenetic-therapy-differ-from-the-light-responses-in-healthy-retina-it-is-unknown-how-altering-retinal-light-responses-via-optogenetic-therapy-changes-visual-responses-in-visual-cortex-and-how-this-affects-visual-perception-here-we-will-examine-visual-cortex-responses-and-visual-perception-in-mice-following-retina-based-optogenetic-therapy-these-results-will-provide-a-multiscale-analysis-providing-crucial-insights-into-how-the-nature-of-retina-based-vision-restoration-affects-its-efficacy","provenance":"brain_canada"},{"id":"G9000742505","name":"ASH HONORS Award 2025: Suraj Bansal","amount":null,"currency":null,"year":2025,"start":null,"end":null,"recipients":[{"id":"I2802654988","name":"Princess Margaret Cancer Centre","country":"CA"}],"parents":[],"funder":"American Society of Hematology","scheme":"ASH HONORS Award: Medical Student","type":"training","topic":null,"source":"https://www.hematology.org/awards/award-recipients/ash-honors-award","provenance":"ash_award_recipients"}],"funding":{"series":[{"currency":"CAD","awards":53,"years":[{"year"